      "id": 46,
      "title": "DM Draft: The Second Age",
      "type": "Generic",
      "categoryId": 4,
      "summary": "The age now running: counted from the morning after the First Fall, in its twenty-sixth year, with the fallen star's husk still silent under the Conclave's seal.",
      "body": "The Second Age is the age now running, counted from [[The First Fall|the Fall]] that ended [[The First Age]].\n\nIt began untidily, the way ages do. The star fell on the last night of the old age, in the season when the count turns over anyway, and the search for what had fallen ran on for months into the new year, before the churches understood what they had found. When the auditors closed the First Age at 1,384 years, they fixed the year already running as the Second Age's first, and the boundary has been clean on paper ever since, whatever it looked like on the ground.\n\nThe age is young, and mostly quiet. The Conclave holds the Fall's dark husk under seal in its vaults, where it has sat silent into its twenty-sixth year, and the churches argue about it at the pace churches argue. The count itself never stopped: the same Ledger, the same calendar, the same keepers' dates, running on into a second age nobody had planned for.\n\nThis history is written in the age's twenty-sixth year.",
